---
/*
 * Ported word for word from the live site's privacy policy (supplied by Holly,
 * 23 Sept 2026), with the address updated on Holly's instruction. Section 10
 * (Apple Health and Health Connect) added word for word on Holly's instruction,
 * 26 Oct 2026. Do not edit the wording here; policy changes are Holly's call.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../config/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How Active AI Ltd collects, uses and protects your personal information, and the rights you have.">
  <section class="band band--chalk">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta label">Active AI Ltd · Version 1 · Reviewed 5th June 2025</p>

      <div class="summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p><strong>Data Controller:</strong> Active AI Ltd, {COMPANY.address}.</p>
        <p>We will only collect personal information that you have voluntarily decided to provide to us or we have recorded from your usage of the Service. We will never sell, rent or give away your personal data to other third parties.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect and process using the Active AI Ltd platform and related services (the "Service"), and the choices and rights you have in connection with your personal information. Active AI Ltd is the Data Controller for this Service.</p>

      <h2>2. Data Protection Framework</h2>
      <p>Active AI Ltd is based in the United Kingdom and is registered with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) as a Data Controller under the UK Data Protection Act and GDPR.</p>

      <h2>3. What Information Do We Collect?</h2>
      <p>We may collect your name, email address, phone number, IP address, activity data, and any other contact details or content which you have provided to us. If you connect an activity tracker we may also collect fitness data including steps, distance, heart rate, sleep data, calories, and activity summaries.</p>

      <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
      <p>We use your personal information to provide the full features of the Service, and to analyse, improve and promote the Service. We will always ask you before processing your personal data in any other way. We use anonymised data to prepare statistics to improve our service.</p>

      <h2>5. Legal Basis</h2>
      <p>Our processing is based on the consent you have voluntarily provided to us.</p>

      <h2>6. Data Sharing</h2>
      <p>We will only share your personal information with our declared data processors: Amazon Web Services, Laravel Forge/Vapor, MailChimp, Google Analytics, Google G Suite, Cloudinary, Pusher, and WeFitter. All sub-processors comply with relevant data protection frameworks.</p>

      <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to be informed, access your data, rectify inaccuracies, request erasure, restrict processing, data portability, object to processing, lodge a complaint, and withdraw consent. Contact us to exercise any of these rights.</p>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>This Service is not directed to users under 18, except where users aged 13–18 have obtained prior parental or guardian consent.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Policy from time to time. You will be notified of significant changes before continuing to use the Service.</p>

      <h2 id="health-data">10. Apple Health and Health Connect</h2>
      <p>You can choose to connect Apple Health (on iPhone) or Health Connect (on Android) to Tuesday. This is optional. Tuesday works without it, and nothing is read until you connect and give permission on your phone.</p>

      <h3>What we read</h3>
      <p>We read your workouts only. For each one we read:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the type of activity, for example a run, a ride or a swim</li>
        <li>when it started and ended</li>
        <li>your moving time</li>
        <li>the distance</li>
        <li>the height climbed</li>
        <li>the name of the app that recorded it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not read heart rate, calories, sleep, your route or location, body measurements, or any other health data. We never write anything to Apple Health or Health Connect.</p>
      <p>When you first connect, we read your workouts from the last 35 days. After that we read new, changed and deleted workouts when you open the app or pull down to refresh.</p>

      <h3>How we use it</h3>
      <p>We use your workouts for one purpose: to work out your Athlete Momentum inside Tuesday. If you also connect Strava or Garmin, your tracker is what your momentum is worked out from, and we keep your Apple Health or Health Connect workouts beside it.</p>

      <h3>Who can see it</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your workouts are never posted to the community feed, and no one else sees their details.</li>
        <li>A workout from Apple Health or Health Connect can count towards your crew’s, rival’s or challenge’s tally of days you were active. That tally is a count of days, and shows no time, distance or other figure from your health data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What we never do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>We never sell this data.</li>
        <li>We never use it for advertising or marketing.</li>
        <li>We never share it with brands, sponsors or other partners.</li>
        <li>We never use it to build profiles of you for anyone else, or pass it to data brokers.</li>
        <li>People at Active AI do not read it, except with your permission, to keep the service secure, or where the law requires it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Where it is kept, and for how long</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>It is stored on our servers, which our hosting providers run on our behalf, and is encrypted in transit. It is not stored in iCloud.</li>
        <li>We keep it while you stay connected.</li>
        <li>If you disconnect in Tuesday’s Settings, we delete everything Apple Health or Health Connect sent us straight away, including any momentum worked out from it. The workouts stay on your phone, and you can connect again at any time.</li>
        <li>If you delete your Tuesday account, it is deleted with everything else.</li>
        <li>You can also turn off Tuesday’s access at any time in the Health app on iPhone, or in Health Connect’s settings on Android.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Health Connect: Limited Use</h3>
      <p>Our use of information received from Health Connect follows the Health Connect Permissions policy, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Active AI Ltd · {COMPANY.address}<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:holly@weareactiveai.com">holly@weareactiveai.com</a> · Tel: <a href="tel:+447771346748">07771 346748</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
  .meta { color: var(--ink-muted); margin: 1rem 0 2rem; }
  .summary { background: var(--white); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0; }
  .summary h2 { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
